course: dictionary
lesson: 8196
title: Restrict: keeping within limits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To restrict something means to keep it within a limit, or to control what people can do or where they can go. Look for clues such as limit, only, allowed, or not allowed.
explain: «Parents restrict screen time» means parents keep the time within a limit, so you cannot use screens for as long as you like. Try swapping in limit or control: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Catching wild parrots for pets is now restricted to protect them.» Here restricted means only allowed in certain ways, to keep the parrots safe. Some films are age-restricted, and some areas are restricted for safety.
fact: Restrict is a verb: to restrict, restricts, restricted, restricting.
fact: The noun is restriction, which means a limit or rule that controls something.
fact: «Restrict» means to keep something within a limit or stop it growing beyond a certain size or amount.
fact: «Restrict» also means to control what people can do or where they can go.
fact: Useful phrases: restrict to, restricted area, age-restricted, restrict access.
exercise: «Children under twelve are not allowed to see this film, because it is age-restricted.» What does age-restricted mean? | Free for everyone | Shown in colour | Very long and boring | *Only allowed for people of a certain age
exercise: «Only staff may enter the back room; it is a restricted area.» What does restricted area mean? | A very big room | *A place only some people are allowed to go | A place with lots of toys | A place to eat lunch
exercise: Mum says, «I will restrict your screen time to one hour.» What does restrict mean here? | Forget about it | Share it with friends | *Keep it within a limit | Make it bigger
test: «Catching wild parrots for pets is now restricted to protect them.» What does restricted suggest here? | *Only allowed in certain ways, to keep them safe | Made bigger and wilder | Made into a pet shop | Easy for everyone to do
test: Which word is the noun form of restrict? | Restricts | Restricting | Restricted | *Restriction
exam: Which sentence uses restrict to mean keep within a limit? | The restrict was painted red and very tall | Restrict means happy | Restrict is a very long word | *The teacher will restrict the game to ten minutes
